// TM-1187 as she stands in 2155: same hull, one cheap decision.
//
// The original VK-H90 (12A) died and was replaced with a secondhand Kirin
// KH-77 — a 16A unit, aftermarket, six years younger than the hull and
// already worn when it arrived. Whoever fitted it did not want to pull the
// engineering trunk, so the heater feed was rerouted through the galley:
// the short ugly way. GALLEY is a 3-way run and now carries four.
//
// BRK-01: 16 + 6 + 0 + 2 + 2 + 1 = 27 on a 25A breaker. It works until the
// heater and the lights are asked for at the same time. Then it doesn't.
ShipFixture(
class: "testudo",
hull_no: "TM-1187",
commissioned: 2149.31,
seed: 0xC0FFEE1187,
rooms: [ (id: "R1", name: "cabin"), (id: "R2", name: "engineering") ],
